5,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,Um... I think we should look at the things that happen every day. I'd like to check the time lost to copying existing records and the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,May,,I agree with Daisuke that we need a reality check. I'll look into the staffing of the coordination group and in-house developer availability to see who is actually going to do the work.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's all well and good to look at the ""floor,"" but we shouldn't ignore the technical hurdles. I'll check network coverage at customer plants and the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I believe we need to be clear about the financial implications before we commit. I will look into the capital budget and software allowance, as well as vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"That sounds like a great plan, everyone! I want to see what we can learn from the past, so I'll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm glad everyone is on board. I just hope that by looking at those logs, we can find a project that actually helps the people struggling with the small things.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. It's easy to get swept up in a fancy pitch, but if the people on the ground are already drowning in work, a new tool might just be another burden.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your concern is noted, but a ""burden"" is usually just a lack of planning. I'm more interested in whether the infrastructure even supports these ideas before we start worrying about the rota.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, planning is only as good as the budget that supports it. If we miscalculate the funding source or the long-term costs, the most well-planned project will still fail.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Kenji,,I think you're all making really important points! I just want to make sure we don't make the same mistakes twice. Let's see what the data tells us!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree with Kenji. I just hope we don't overlook the small, repetitive problems that the data might not show as ""failures,"" but still make the work hard for everyone.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,May,,"That's why I'm checking the staffing, Daisuke. If the coordination group is already stretched thin, they can't just ""absorb"" a new project. We need to know who is actually available to manage this.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, checking staffing is a start, but it's useless if the project requires a network that doesn't exist. I'm more concerned with the physical and technical constraints that usually get ignored until it's too late.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, technical constraints are critical, but they are often tied to how we pay for the solution. A fixed-fee build is a different risk than a per-user license. We must understand the cost structure first.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm just so excited to see what we find! I think if we combine all these different views—the money, the people, and the history—we'll definitely pick the best project for everyone!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I hope so, Kenji. I'll just wait for the results now. I really want us to find something that makes the daily work a little easier for everyone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,May,,"I'm with you, Daisuke. Let's just make sure we don't let the ""impressive"" options blind us to the actual capacity of our team. I'm looking forward to seeing the numbers.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Numbers are fine, but they don't tell the whole story. I'm looking for the gaps between the promise and the reality. Let's see if the data actually supports the ambitions of these proposals.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. Data provides the necessary boundaries for our decision. Once we have the facts regarding the budget and the technical constraints, we can evaluate the proposals with a rational perspective. I am ready to proceed.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,Me too! I can't wait to see what the records show. Let's get the information and figure this out together! I'm ready!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
