35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that people in the depot and planning office lose nearly an hour every day just copying records. Also, eleven deliveries were misrouted because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"That's exactly what I feared, Daisuke. My findings are just as grim: the coordination group is understaffed and still doing logs by hand, and our in-house developers are completely unavailable until Q3. We have no one to build or manage this.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we're facing a reality check. I found that half of the customer plants have terrible network coverage and device approval is a nightmare. Also, broad tools requiring daily entry from everyone usually fail.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial situation is equally restrictive. The capital budget is frozen, meaning we can only use the recurring software allowance. Furthermore, per-head licenses will increase costs as we scale, whereas fixed-fee work remains stable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, that's a lot of information! I also saw that broad tools requiring daily entry from everyone usually get dropped, and most cross-unit standardization efforts failed because they had no owner. We really need something focused!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I feel like the data shows we really need to fix those daily losses. The copying and the misrouted deliveries are happening right now, and they seem like things we could actually solve.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I agree, but we have to be careful. With no developers available and the coordination group already drowning in manual logs, we can't pick anything that adds more administrative work to their plates.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, you're finally seeing the point. If we pick a project that requires broad adoption or complex setup, it'll be dead in a year. We need something narrow and technically feasible.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree. Given the frozen capital budget, we must avoid any project requiring a large upfront investment. We should prioritize solutions that fit within the recurring software allowance and avoid per-head licensing to prevent future budget spikes.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that's a great point about the budget! And @Shunichi, since we know broad tools fail, maybe we should look for something that helps a specific group without needing everyone to use it every day?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think that makes sense. If we can find a way to stop the copying and the address errors without making more work for the coordination group, it would really help the people on the floor.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, exactly. But remember, we can't rely on our in-house developers. Whatever we choose must be something we can implement without them, or something that doesn't require a massive technical build-out from scratch.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, precisely. And we must avoid anything relying on customer-site connectivity, given the signal issues I found. A ""fancy"" app is useless if it can't connect. We need a focused, low-maintenance tool.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, your point about connectivity is vital. Combined with the budget freeze, we must avoid high-risk technical dependencies. A solution with a fixed-fee structure and low operational overhead is the only rational choice.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm starting to see a pattern! We need something that doesn't need everyone's daily input, doesn't rely on bad networks, and doesn't cost a fortune to scale. I wonder if any of the candidates fit all those rules?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I just hope the candidates have something that addresses the address errors and the copying. It would be so sad if we had the data but couldn't find a way to actually help the staff.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, don't lose heart. We have a very clear set of constraints now. As long as we don't pick a project that pretends our staff have infinite free time, we'll be making the right choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be realistic. We need a project that is narrow in scope, avoids the nightmare of customer-site connectivity, and doesn't require a small army of developers or users to maintain it. Anything else is just a fantasy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. We must be disciplined. We need a solution that fits the recurring software allowance, avoids per-head licensing, and requires minimal internal staffing. Let us see which candidate survives these rational constraints.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready too! It feels like we've built a great checklist together. I can't wait to see the candidates and help everyone pick the one that actually works and lasts!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
