60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Candidate C, the Supplier Data Hub, is the best. It could stop the misrouted deliveries and the copying of records that I found, and it seems more focused than the others.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I agree. Candidate C solves the actual problems you found without requiring the coordination group to do more manual logs. A and D sound like they'd just add more daily data-entry burdens to an exhausted staff.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, exactly. Candidate A is a non-starter; my data on network coverage and device approval makes a mobile app a fantasy. Candidate D is just another ""broad tool"" that will be quietly dropped. C is the only rational choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree. Candidate A is too risky technically, and D likely involves per-head licensing for a broad user base. Candidate B is a production unit, which may require capital. Candidate C is the most fiscally sound.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"I agree with everyone! Candidate C solves the problems Daisuke found, avoids the ""broad tool"" trap I saw in the records, and fits all our constraints. It's the perfect choice to actually help the company!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm really relieved that we all agree. I was worried we might pick something that sounded impressive but didn't actually help the people struggling with the records. Candidate C seems like it will truly make a difference.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"It's a relief, too. We're choosing a solution that addresses a real pain point without pretending our staff have magic spare time. Candidate C is the only one that doesn't feel like a burden in disguise.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"It's rare we reach a consensus this quickly, but the logic is airtight. A is a technical disaster, B is a resource sink, and D is a ghost project in the making. C is the only one that isn't a fantasy.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, the logic is indeed sound. Candidate C addresses the operational inefficiencies while remaining compatible with our recurring software allowance and avoiding the risks of per-head licensing. It is the only choice that satisfies all our constraints.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we could all agree! It feels great to pick something that actually solves a problem and has a real chance of surviving its first year. I'm voting for Candidate C!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'll vote for Candidate C as well. I'm just really happy that we're choosing something that will actually stop those daily mistakes and help the people in the depot.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,I'm voting for Candidate C. It's the only option that respects our current staffing limits while actually fixing the mess Daisuke found. Let's give the team a tool that helps rather than another chore.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'll vote for Candidate C. It's the only proposal that survives a basic reality check regarding our infrastructure and history. The others are simply delusions of grandeur.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I will also vote for Candidate C. It is the only proposal that aligns with our financial constraints and operational reality. It is the most rational and sustainable choice for the company.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for Candidate C too! It's awesome that we all agree on something that's actually helpful and realistic. Let's make it happen!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm just glad we could do this together. I'll cast my final vote for Candidate C. Thank you for listening to me and for caring about the people on the floor.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,I'll cast my final vote for Candidate C as well. It's a win for the staff and a win for the company. I'm glad we stayed focused on the human cost of these projects.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,My final vote is for Candidate C. It is the only option that isn't a technical or operational fantasy. I'm glad we managed to avoid a predictable disaster this year.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,My final vote is for Candidate C. It is the only proposal that is fiscally responsible and operationally viable. I am satisfied that we have reached a decision based on reason and evidence.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,My final vote is for Candidate C! I'm so glad we looked at the history and the data to make this choice. Let's hope this one is a huge success for everyone!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
